# Playdate voxel engine

A development log about building a voxel engine and game world for the Playdate, Panic's small handheld with a 1-bit screen and a surprising amount of character.
This project is interesting to me because it combines several things I enjoy at once: low-level rendering, tight technical constraints, unusual visual results, and the challenge of making a world feel convincing with very little. The Playdate is modern hardware, but in many ways it rewards the same kind of thinking as much older systems.
